        <div id="what-it-does" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. What a Whole House Water Filter Does (and What It Does Not)
          </h2>

          <p>
            The best whole house water filter is the one matched to your water source and the problem you can taste, smell or see. Before comparing systems, it helps to be clear about what a whole house filter is for.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Point of Entry, Not Point of Use</h3>

          <p>
            A whole house filter installs on the main water line, usually just after the shut-off valve and before the water heater, so every tap, shower and appliance gets filtered water. That is called point-of-entry treatment. A pitcher, faucet filter or under-sink system treats only the water at one tap, which is point-of-use treatment. Our guide to <a href="/best-water-filtration-system-for-home/">water filtration systems for home</a> compares both approaches.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What It Usually Removes</h3>

          <p>
            Most whole house systems target sediment, rust, and chlorine taste and odor. The better ones add KDF media, catalytic carbon for chloramine, or a polyphosphate stage for scale. Removing chlorine at the main means your showers stop smelling of a swimming pool, which is the reason most city water households buy one.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What It Leaves Behind</h3>

          <p>
            Whole house carbon systems keep dissolved minerals in the water. The Aquasana and A. O. Smith listings both say they do not reduce total dissolved solids, and A. O. Smith adds that its filter does not treat sulfur or iron. None of the systems here is a water softener, and none of them disinfects water. If you need those, you need a different product as well. For scale control without salt, a <a href="/best-water-conditioner/">water conditioner</a> using TAC media pairs well with a carbon filter.
          </p>
        </div>

